---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Trauma Therapy in Provo & Utah County | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Trauma therapy in Provo, Orem, & Sandy, Utah. Heal from childhood, abuse, or relational trauma with EMDR, IFS & Somatic approaches. Free 15-min consult."}>
<section class="sec t-bright h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-47-9c7b1b.jpg" alt="A therapy group sits in a circle in a bright room full of plants at Tangible Therapy in Utah" style="object-position:50% 50%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.6"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:10">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/5/6/23;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Trauma Therapy</h1><p class="lg ta-center">Trauma therapy that helps you reclaim your voice and your peace</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/10/8/18;--m:8/2/10/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Start Trauma Counseling Today</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:14;--mrows:18">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/6/12;--m:2/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>When your body keeps the score</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/14/14/25;--m:12/2/19/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/tangible-13-09bc29.jpg" alt="A woman in a light blue blazer and beige skirt is sitting in a cozy living room, holding a pen and notebook, engaged in a virtual conversation on her laptop, with a child visible on the screen." width="2093" height="1406" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/13/12;--m:4/2/12/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Trauma doesn’t always look like one big event. Sometimes it’s years of subtle harm, emotional neglect, or unsafe environments that train your body to stay on high alert.</p><p>You might feel numb, disconnected, anxious, or stuck in survival mode. You might have memories that won’t fade — or no memory at all, only the aftermath. Trauma therapy helps you understand these responses, reconnect with your body, and start healing from the inside out.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/2/17/13;--m:1/2/8/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/tangible-32-9dd014.jpg" alt="a female therapist in a light shirt at Tangible Therapy. Smiling and sitting across from a woman while they do trauma Therapy." width="2203" height="1702" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/15/6/26;--m:9/2/12/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>We support survivors of all kinds of trauma</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/15/17/25;--m:12/2/20/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>No matter what happened — or how long ago — we’re here. We work with clients who have experienced:</p><ul><li><p>Childhood trauma or developmental neglect</p></li><li><p>Physical, emotional, or sexual abuse</p></li><li><p>Medical or birth trauma</p></li><li><p>Identity-based or systemic trauma</p></li><li><p>Domestic violence or relationship abuse</p></li><li><p>Religious trauma or high-control environments</p></li><li><p>Accidents, disasters, or sudden loss</p></li></ul><p>You don’t need a “trauma story” that sounds dramatic. If your nervous system hasn’t felt safe in a long time, that’s enough.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-white-bold h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:11;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/16/12/26;--m:12/2/20/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:40px"><img src="/images/therapy-green-03bc1b.jpg" alt="a female trauma therapist in a light shirt at Tangible Therapy in Provo, Utah. Smiling and sitting across from a woman while they do Therapy." width="2500" height="1932" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/6/13;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>You don’t have to go back to who you were</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/9/12;--m:3/2/10/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p><span class="c-accent">Trauma changes us. But healing <em>is</em> possible. With the right support, you can feel more connected to yourself, more in control of your life, and more hopeful about what comes next.</span></p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:9/2/11/8;--m:10/2/12/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Schedule an Appointment Today</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Trauma Therapists</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/5/17/24;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth/trauma" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:2vmax;padding-bottom:0vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Understand your triggers and survival responses</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Reduce flashbacks, panic, or dissociation</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Reconnect with your body in a safe, supported way</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Release shame, self-blame, and stuck emotional patterns</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Rebuild trust with yourself and others</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Begin to feel grounded, whole, and calm again</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#acb9ac" /></section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>What if I don’t remember what happened to me?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s common. Many people with trauma have partial or no memory of the event(s). We can still work with your symptoms, emotions, and body responses in a gentle and effective way.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is trauma therapy the same as PTSD treatment?</summary><div class="rte"><p>They overlap. You don’t need a PTSD diagnosis to benefit from trauma therapy. We work with both single-incident and complex trauma — including long-term or developmental experiences.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do I have to talk about everything that happened?</summary><div class="rte"><p>No. You’re always in control of what you share and when. Many trauma-focused therapies don’t require detailed retelling to be effective. We follow your lead, not a script.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/11/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>What if my trauma is still ongoing or recent?</summary><div class="rte"><p>We offer stabilization-focused support for clients dealing with ongoing stress or danger. You don’t have to wait until things are “calm” to begin healing. We’ll meet you where you are.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is trauma therapy retraumatizing?</summary><div class="rte"><p>It shouldn’t be. At Tangible, we always move slowly and center your sense of safety. If anything feels too intense, we pause. You set the pace. Always.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
